type: dataset
title: "Alexander Grothendieck: A Life in Three Universes"
abstract: "Few twentieth-century mathematicians changed so many working assumptions as Alexander Grothendieck (1928–2014). Across twelve Parts and seventy-two chapters, this biography follows him from a family archive whose smallest facts are contested, through camps, schools and postwar seminars, to the collective construction of a new geometry; then a rupture over military funding, activism, university classrooms, private manuscripts and a village in the Ariège; and, after his death, two archives, new editions and the mathematics that continues. It follows documents before symbols, chronology before destiny, and relations before essence."
